# system-of-record-leads-physical-state

The IMS (inventory management system) is the authoritative source of truth for lot location. Physical state changes must always be preceded and authorized by a confirmed IMS transaction — never concurrent with or after. Physical actions that outrun IMS confirmation create unrecoverable divergence between recorded and actual state, which corrupts downstream traceability and audit trails.

## Procedures
- Submit the IMS pre-move location update transaction before touching the lot.
- Wait for explicit confirmation of the transaction (not just submission) before initiating physical movement.
- If IMS confirmation is delayed or unavailable, hold the lot in place — do not move and update IMS retroactively.

## Conventions
- IMS confirmation is a hard prerequisite, not a concurrent or post-action step.
- Retroactive IMS updates after a physical move are a process violation, not a recovery path.

